menu "usb_device test options"

    config TEST_USB_HOST_ATTACHED
        bool "Run ONLY the bus-attaching tests"
        default n
        help
            The default build runs every case that does not touch the USB bus, so
            it is safe on a board whose only console is USB-Serial/JTAG.

            With this set, app_main() runs only the [needs_usb_host] cases, which
            call usb_device_start(). On the ESP32-S3 that switches the PHY to OTG
            and the USJ console disappears until the board is physically replugged
            (CON-09, TBD-009). The Unity output goes with it, so the result has to
            be read from the host side - see the case's own comment.

endmenu
